msgid "Security fixes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we released Quarkus 3.33.4, our next maintenance release for the 3.33 "
"LTS stream."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This release contains bugfixes, documentation updates, and security fixes."
msgstr ""

msgid "It should be a safe upgrade for anyone already using 3.33."
msgstr ""

msgid "This release fixes the following CVEs:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus and direct dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-89407[CVE-2026-89407] - FasterXML "
"jackson-core: Denial of Service via quadratic regex backtracking in number "
"validation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-89425[CVE-2026-89425] - FasterXML "
"jackson-core: Denial of Service via unbounded error-token accumulation in "
"`UTF8DataInputJsonParser`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-91777[CVE-2026-91777] - FasterXML "
"jackson-databind: Denial of Service via quadratic-time forward-reference "
"resolution for `@JsonIdentityInfo`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-91776[CVE-2026-91776] - FasterXML "
"jackson-databind: Denial of Service via unbounded deserializer cache growth "
"for unrecognized polymorphic type IDs"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-84939[CVE-2026-84939] - Apache "
"FreeMarker: Path traversal via malformed locale identifier"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94449[CVE-2026-94449] - Quarkus "
"SmallRye Fault Tolerance: Memory leak in `@ApplyGuard` leads to Denial of "
"Service"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82617[CVE-2026-82617] - Apache "
"OpenNLP: Denial of Service via super-linear regex backtracking in built-in "
"name finders"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-68497[CVE-2026-68497] - Jackson-"
"databind: Denial of Service via unbounded number parsing for `Duration`/"
"`XMLGregorianCalendar`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-89059[CVE-2026-89059] - RESTEasy: "
"Denial of Service via unbounded memory allocation in `IIOImageProvider`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-93432[CVE-2026-93432] - Quarkus "
"Qute: Cross-Site Scripting via missing content-type propagation in `{#eval}` "
"sub-templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59949[CVE-2026-59949] - LZ4 Java: "
"Denial of Service via native XXHash crash on invalid byte array ranges"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59296[CVE-2026-59296] - Micrometer:"
" Metrics injection/spoofing via unsanitized newline characters in StatsD and "
"logging registries"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59295[CVE-2026-59295] - Micrometer:"
" Denial of Service via unbounded memory leak in `HttpAsyncClient` "
"instrumentation"
msgstr ""

msgid "Platform updates"
msgstr ""

msgid "This release includes Quarkus CXF 3.33.12."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-cxf/dev/release-notes/3.33.10."
"html[Release notes] for Quarkus CXF 3.33.10"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Release notes for Quarkus CXF 3.33.11 and 3.33.12 are not yet published at "
"the time of publishing this announcement"
msgstr ""

msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.33, we recommend updating to the latest version of "
"the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.33."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/3.33.4[the "
"full changelog of 3.33.4 on GitHub]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
